# Explorer's Cache: the activated ability is sorcery speed and takes any creature, the opponent's too. Turn 2, with Bot2's Ornithopter on the
# stack, Bot1 cannot move a counter (not Bot1's turn, the stack not empty: CR 602.5d for "activate only as a sorcery"). On turn 3 it moves
# one onto Bot2's Ornithopter, so that creature has a +1/+1 counter but is not Bot1's. Wrath of God then destroys Bot1's own Ornithopter, which has no
# counter, and Bot2's, which has one but is not "a creature you control" (CR 603.10a looks back to its controller, Bot2): neither triggers the Cache,
# which keeps its single remaining counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Explorer's Cache
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Plains
Ornithopter
Plains
Wrath of God
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

